- The zero linear map $T: V -> W$, defined by $T(bold(x)) = bold(0)$ for all $bold(x) in V$, has $im T = {bold(0)}$ and $ker T = V$.

- The identity map $T: V -> V$, defined by $T(bold(x)) = bold(x)$, has $im T = V$ and $ker T = {bold(0)}$.

- On $RR^2$, the map with
  $
    x'_1 &= 2x_1 + x_2, \
    x'_2 &= x_1 - 4x_2,
  $
  is linear; here $im T = {lambda vec(2, 1) + mu vec(1, -3): lambda, mu in RR} = RR^2$ and $ker T = {bold(0)}$.
